# GitHub application configuration

## Browser sign-in: required

Register a GitHub OAuth App OR a GitHub App using the user authorization-code
flow. Homepage: https://{{.Requirements.Azure.Parameters.functionAppName}}.azurewebsites.net/
Authorization callback: https://{{.Requirements.Azure.Parameters.functionAppName}}.azurewebsites.net/auth/callback

Set githubClientId and put its client secret in the referenced githubClientSecret
secret. No PAT or pasted user token is supported.
Sign-in GitHub Apps need expiring user tokens; organization/team checks require
Members: read and an approved installation in each allowed organization.
Approve classic OAuth App organization access where restrictions apply.
Ordinary classic login uses read:org read:user, not repo. Directly allowed
users do not require organization membership lookups. Test allowed AND
disallowed identities. App installation does not widen CAO policy.

## Collection App: {{if eq .Topology.Features.Acquisition "collector"}}required, separate credential boundary{{else}}not selected{{end}}

{{if eq .Topology.Features.Acquisition "collector"}}
Use App ID {{.Requirements.Azure.Parameters.collectorGithubAppId}}, NOT an
OAuth client ID. Configure HTTPS webhooks at
https://{{.Requirements.Azure.Parameters.functionAppName}}.azurewebsites.net/api/github/webhook
Store its RSA PEM in collectorPrivateKey and the same high-entropy HMAC secret
in GitHub and githubWebhookSecret.

Enable Workflow run events and retain installation/installation-repositories
lifecycle deliveries. Review the exact ingestion evidence: Actions: read for
runs/artifacts, Contents: read for reviewed workflow/policy inputs and
Metadata: read for selected repositories. Other evidence needs separately
reviewed read permissions, never a speculative write/admin grant.

Install only on reviewed repositories. Verify signature admission, completion,
installation scope and uninstall/removal behavior. Enrollment, reviewed
inventory and CAO policy remain separate authorities.
The public Function App receives only the webhook secret, never the App
private key. Collection workers hold installation-scoped credentials.
{{else}}
Actions snapshot ingestion needs no collection App here. Existing
control-repository workflow Apps remain under their existing reviewed policy;
this generator neither creates nor expands them.
{{end}}

{{if .Optional}}
See OPTIONAL-FEATURES.md for additional archive sign-in and separate gateway
receiving/dispatch Apps. Never reuse their private keys in the Functions process.
{{end}}

Hosted CLI and token-broker execution Apps are NOT enabled by the baseline.
Live safe-output writes require their own reviewed implementation and authority.
ADX needs separate Entra setup/runtime principals, not a GitHub App.
No App creation, installation, permission acceptance or live check is automated.
